WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.7 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
RACI and process ownership

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
RACI shows who does, who owns, who advises and who is told, so small teams ask instead of assume.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.170
RACI is a simple table that shows who does what in a process or decision. Each person in a row gets a letter for their kind of involvement.

4
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:26.170
The four letters

5
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:35.648
R · Responsible: Does the work or prepares the decision. One or more people. For example: At the youth club, a volunteer drafts the summer programme.

6
00:00:35.648 --> 00:00:46.237
A · Accountable: Owns the result and signs it off; can say no. Exactly one per row. For example: The founder who leads activities approves the final summer programme.

7
00:00:46.237 --> 00:00:56.456
C · Consulted: Gives input before the work is finished; two-way. As few as possible. For example: Two parents comment on the draft programme before it is fixed.

8
00:00:56.456 --> 00:01:07.504
I · Informed: Told about the outcome; one-way. Anyone who needs to know. For example: The co-founder handling money hears the final dates to plan the budget.

9
00:01:07.904 --> 00:01:08.504
Why it helps small teams

10
00:01:08.504 --> 00:01:14.178
1. Small teams assume rather than ask; a RACI makes it visible.

11
00:01:14.178 --> 00:01:19.111
2. One Accountable per row ends arguments about who decides.

12
00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:25.044
3. New people see at once how recurring work flows.

13
00:01:25.444 --> 00:01:26.044
Where you will use it

14
00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:31.719
1. Recurring work: the annual plan, funding bids or pitches, recruiting, complaints.

15
00:01:31.719 --> 00:01:36.281
2. Your process owners and SOPs in Module 5.

16
00:01:36.281 --> 00:01:42.585
3. Your meetings: check the table whenever a hand-off is unclear.

17
00:01:42.985 --> 00:01:43.585
What to avoid

18
00:01:43.585 --> 00:01:49.259
Two Accountables in one row, which means nobody really owns it.

19
00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:53.822
Too many Consulted, which slows every decision down.

20
00:01:53.822 --> 00:02:00.126
Writing it once and never updating it when roles change.

21
00:02:00.726 --> 00:02:02.526
You build a RACI for five key processes in your first year.

22
00:02:02.526 --> 00:02:06.526
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:08.026 --> 00:02:11.126
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
